<title>USA: S&amp;P says Argentina outlook rumors were &quot;false&quot;.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P says Argentina outlook rumors were &quot;false&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard and Poor's Corp said Tuesday that published reports in Buenos Aires of an imminent change in Argentina's outlook were completely false.</p>
<p>&quot;The rumor is totally false,&quot; Lacey Gallagher, director of sovereign ratings at S&amp;P, told Reuters. &quot;It's totally false and unfounded, There's no basis to it.&quot;</p>
<p>S&amp;P currently maintains a BB-minus foreign currency debt rating with a stable outlook for Argentina.</p>
<p>The Argentine paper Ambito Financiero wrote Monday that S&amp;P would change its outlook to negative.</p>
<p>-- George Lerner, 212-859-1671</p>
</text>
